  "notes": "Contract authored 2026-08-23 during the MDN-shape upgrade of this previously legacy-unassessed page. Every value-stage claim was re-derived from the current editor's drafts (css-backgrounds-3, css-ui-4, css-multicol — normative sentences quoted verbatim in #syntax) plus CSSOM's resolved-value list, and cross-checked against the ChromeStatus summary's explicit statement that resolved values change only for outline-width and column-rule-width. The upgrade corrects a factual error in the earlier revision, which claimed getComputedStyle().borderWidth returns the authored value in Chrome 147+ — css-backgrounds-3 defines border-width's resolved value as the used value, still 0px when the style is none/hidden; the correction is noted visibly on the page. BCD records base property support only, not the decoupling — the compat table separates verbatim BCD columns from the interim ChromeStatus-sourced change column."
